{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they took their cattle, etc.</b> The reason it did not say this at the beginning of the journey, when it said (Genesis 46:1) ״וַיִּסַּע״ etc. — perhaps it is because at first they set out only to escort Jacob and also to see Joseph's face; but after the prophetic vision was revealed to them, it became known to them that El Elyon concurred that they should sojourn in Egypt until the day He would wish to bring them up from there — and as I explained in the verse ״אָנֹכִי אֵרֵד וְאָנֹכִי״ — upon this they agreed to take with them all their cattle and their clothing, etc. Scripture also informs us that even though they knew that HaShem had there ordained the exile, they did not stiffen their necks, nor did they refrain — heaven forfend — from fulfilling the debt-bond of exile; rather they bore their little ones, etc., and they came to Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:01.038290825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}